      "problem": "Express $\\sqrt[3]{4^2}$ using a fractional exponent.",
      "worked_solution": "The radical $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ can be written using a fractional exponent as $x^{1/n}.$\n\nComparing $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ with $\\sqrt[3]{4^2},$ we get $x = 4^2$ and $n = 3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{4^2} = \\left(4^2\\right)^{1/3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the power law for exponents, we have\n\n$$\n\\left(4^2\\right)^{1/3} = 4^{2/3}.\n$$",
